[0.403, "o", "Build a small Python CLI named `csvsummary.py` using only the standard library.\r\n"]
[0.458, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.513, "o", "- Read a CSV file from a positional argument, or stdin when no file is given.\r\n"]
[0.568, "o", "- Print JSON with `rows`, `columns` (the header names), and `numeric_totals`.\r\n"]
[0.623, "o", "- Sum a column only when every non-empty value is a finite number. Ignore empty\r\n"]
[0.678, "o", "  cells; omit columns with no numbers. Reject rows with the wrong number of cells.\r\n"]
[0.733, "o", "- Provide `--help` and useful errors with nonzero exit codes.\r\n"]
[0.788, "o", "- Add `test_csvsummary.py` covering files, stdin, empty input, quoted fields,\r\n"]
[0.843, "o", "  missing values, non-numeric columns, and malformed rows. Run `python3 -m unittest -v`.\r\n"]
[0.898, "o", "- Verify `sales.csv` reports 3 rows, columns `name` and `amount`, and an amount\r\n"]
[0.953, "o", "  total of 35.5. Add a short README with usage and test commands.\r\n"]
[1.008, "o", "\r\n"]
[1.063, "o", "Finish only after the tests and the sample command pass.\r\n"]
[4.563, "o", ""]
